We are converting groovy from 1.1 to 2.0. We need to make use of HmacSHA256. 

 We can no longer use library: org.apache.commons.codec.binary.Hex 
 In groovy 1.1 our script was working. 
 This sample script does not run: 
 package script.v2 
 import com.sap.it.script.v2.api.Message 
 def Message processData(Message message) { 
 try { 
 message.setBody(javax.crypto.Mac.getInstance("HmacSHA256").getAlgorithm()) 
 } 
 catch (Exception e) { 
 message.setBody(e.getClass().getName() + ": " + e.getMessage()) 
 } 
 return message 
 } 
 We get error: java.lang.Exception: class javax.crypto.Mac (in unnamed module &#64;0x4123dbf4) cannot access class sun.security.util.Debug 
 Who can help?
